/*
A .d.ts file, also known as a TypeScript Declaration File, is a special type of file in TypeScript that contains only type information. The "d" in .d.ts stands for "declaration."
Unlike regular .ts files, which contain both type definitions and executable code and are compiled into JavaScript, .d.ts files contain no executable code and are not compiled into JavaScript. Their sole purpose is to describe the "shape" or "interface" of existing code, typically JavaScript libraries or modules, to enable TypeScript's type-checking capabilities.
*/
